  url           = {https://doi.org/10.1145/3229631.3264660},
  abstract      = {Significant effort is currently being invested on enhancing digitization in all aspects of industrial processes and manufacturing on the quest for the next transformational change towards sustainable manufacturing and the factories of the future. This vision, commonly termed as Industry 4.0, is at the core of a number of funded projects in Europe. This short paper briefly reports experiences from the EU-funded project DISRUPT and focuses on the identification of some key challenges in the interplay between Industry 4.0 and High Performance Computing.},
